WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.500
Step eight judges the parallel
run on day thirty's snapshot.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.636
In the fixtures, day thirty
is after the cutover,

3
00:00:06.636 --> 00:00:11.538
so each legacy login reads as already
cut over: cutover-ready, four of four.

4
00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:16.649
Step nine dry-runs the rollback, before
the cutover, so its record exists first.

5
00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:21.262
It would grant connect sequel back to the
groups, and enable the superseded logins.

6
00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:23.312
Step ten dry-runs the cutover.

7
00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:28.099
Users and SQL logins are disabled,
and groups are denied connect sequel.

8
00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:31.495
The Windows admin group leaves
the sys-admin role first,

9
00:00:31.495 --> 00:00:34.225
because a deny doesn't
bind sys-admin members.

10
00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:37.990
Nothing is dropped, which is why
the rollback can reverse it at once.
